We Are:

RTB House is a next-generation performance demand-side platform (DSP) that uses proprietary Deep Learning AI algorithms to help brands grow. The company is the market leader in driving performance using Deep Learning across the entire purchase funnel.&nbsp;

Founded in 2012 and now operating in 90+ markets, RTB House has always been private-by-design. It embraces first-party advertising and a relentless approach to innovation. RTB House offers end-to-end Deep Learning-powered AdTech products and solutions to maximize conversion, drive new customer acquisition, create engagement, and fuel long-term demand for a global base of clients.

In 2026, RTB House launched rtb.com, a self-service platform specifically designed to allow small and medium-sized businesses and agencies to deploy auto-built creatives and maximize performance on any budget.

Why RTB House?

If you are looking for a place where you can draw on your consultative problem-solving skills and technical understanding to ensure clients’ performance marketing goals are met, then RTB House might be the right fit for you.&nbsp;

About the role:

As a Technical Account Support Manager in the Central team, you will combine your technical expertise with consultative problem-solving to hit our clients' performance marketing targets. Day to day, you will lead campaign optimization across e-commerce websites and mobile apps to consistently drive measurable impact.&nbsp;

You Will:

• Adjust campaign parameters directly or indirectly using automatic tools to influence campaign performance results;

• Propose solutions for tools and processes to increase efficiency and effectiveness;

• Work closely with the automation team and developers to use deterministic and AI solutions to make daily tasks as automated as possible;

• Look for improvements on the campaign implementations at scale;

• Serve as the primary technical point of contact for non-technical stakeholders in multiple regions.

Desired Experience:

• About 2+ years of experience in online technology, e-commerce and/or digital advertising;

• About 2 years of experience in a Technical Account Manager role in any region running performance campaigns;

• Fluent English (C1 level);

• Basic knowledge of HTML and JavaScript;

• Experience with debugging tools (e.g. Google Chrome DevTools), Google Tag Manager;&nbsp;

• Experience in using Google Analytics 4, MMPs (Appsflyer, Adjust, Branch);

• Strong analytical skills;

• Good time management skills and attention to detail;

• Ability to solve problems efficiently;

• High level of motivation and willingness to learn and improve daily workload by using automations.

We Offer:

• Stable, long-term cooperation based on a B2B contract or contract of mandate;

• Collaboration in a truly international environment with group headquarters in Poland, offering direct access to central decision-makers and cross-functional product/tech teams;

• Opportunity to contribute to ambitious projects within a fast-growing global organization, shaping how technical solutions drive performance across markets;

• Continuous hands-on development with modern ad tech, analytics, and automation tools, with full support for your ideas to streamline daily workflows.

Apply now!

You don't need to tick every box to apply. If you are passionate about digital marketing, send us your CV, and we'll review it.

